  "question": {
    "text": "Two polaroids <math> <mi>A</mi> </math> and <math> <mi>B</mi> </math> are placed with their polaroid axes <math><msup><mrow><mn>30</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi></mrow></msup></math> to each other as shown in the figure. A plane polarised light passes through the polaroid <math> <mi>A</mi> </math> and after passing through it, intensity of light becomes <math><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math>. What is the intensity of finally transmitted light, after passing through the polaroid <math> <mi>B</mi> </math>?<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0048_951bc65a7346.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 172px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>0.75</mn><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>0.866</mn><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>0.25</mn><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>0.5</mn><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "The intensity <math><mi>I</mi></math> of the transmitted light varies directly as the square of the cosine of the angle between the transmission direction of polariser and the&nbsp;analyser.<br /><br /><math><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></math><br /><br />Intensity of finally transmitted light after passing through the polaroid B is given by <math><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></math> (Intensity)<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><msub> <mi>I</mi> <mn>0</mn> </msub> <mo>⋅</mo><msup> <mrow> <mi>cos</mi></mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <msup> <mrow> <mn>30</mn></mrow> <mi>o</mi> </msup> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.75</mn><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math><br /><br />where, <math><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math> is the maximum intensity of transmitted light."
  }
}